Version 1.9.7-alpha
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-08-01

Notes:
 * First tilix-next release, marked alpha: bug fixes and small features
   picked up from gnunn1/tilix's open issues and pull requests while
   that project looks for maintainers.

Features:
 * Add ClipboardPrompt trigger action, a safe alternative to OSC 52:
   matches visible marker text (not raw escape sequences), decodes it,
   and shows an InfoBar with Copy/Ignore buttons, never writing to the
   clipboard without an explicit click. Includes contrib/tilix-copy.sh
   helper script
 * Add optional Sixel image protocol support, letting programs draw real
   images directly in the terminal (img2sixel, chafa -f sixel, etc.).
   Off by default, enabled per profile under Compatibility.
   This also required fixing VTE itself, which decodes and stores sixel
   images but never draws them, leaving a correctly-sized blank gap
   where the picture should be: patches/vte-draw-sixel-images.patch
   supplies the missing drawing code (43 lines, calling VTE's own
   already-written Image::paint()), and contrib/build-vte-sixel.sh
   builds a patched VTE into a private prefix without touching the
   system one. See the README and patches/README.md.
   Note that no stable VTE release contains sixel at all: upstream
   strips the sixel sources before every release and restores them
   afterwards, so 0.76.x through 0.84.1 ship without them and the
   enable-sixel API is a silent no-op there
 * Add GitHub Dark color scheme
 * Add "Scale (fit)" background image mode
 * Add option to remap Ctrl+Backspace (e.g. to Control-W, delete word)
 * Add "Clear" action to clear terminal output while keeping the
   current command line intact

Bugfixes:
 * Fix the entire Triggers feature (UpdateTitle, SendText,
   SendNotification, etc.) never firing on any modern/stock VTE: the
   contents-changed signal was wired up behind a check for a signal
   that only ever existed on old, distro-patched VTE builds, and
   gtk-d's getTextRange() wrapper always returns empty text on current
   VTE due to a deprecated parameter it can't avoid passing
 * Fix crash on OSC 7 sequences with hostnames GLib rejects (e.g.
   starting with a digit, or containing "_"), such as from conda or
   container shells
 * Fix crash opening Keyboard Shortcuts on systems where GtkBuilder
   hadn't already seen GtkShortcutsWindow registered
 * Fix invisible drag-icon window blocking clicks after an interrupted
   title-bar drag
 * Fix crash when a terminal title contains an unescaped "&"
 * Fix install.sh reporting the wrong missing package for some commands
 * Fix build failing at link time with undefined references to
   inflate/deflate/etc. (zlib wasn't linked explicitly)
 * Work around a dmd template-emission bug that could break builds

Miscellaneous:
 * Spanish (es) translation completed to 100%
 * po/LINGUAS fixed to include locale files that existed on disk but
   weren't being shipped (da, et, hi, ka, pt, ta)
 * README rewritten to reflect tilix-next as an actively maintained fork

Contributors:
 YadeWira, Tim Purschke, algj, Robert Ruse, Ruby Lazuli,
 Andrei Horodniceanu, Hiroki Noda, taoky

Version 1.9.6
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2023-11-08

Features:
 * Add close button to search box
 * Replace variables in custom link commands
 * Follow system color-scheme for default theme-variant

Bugfixes:
 * nautilus: Don't import a specific version
 * nautilus: Add compatibility with Nautilus 43
 * nautilus: Avoid shell injection in open-tilix plugin
 * Drop manpage country names
 * Replace std.xml with GMarkup-based parser
 * icon: Fix up prompt pictogram alignment
 * Fix GLib critical warnings on startup

Miscellaneous:
 * Change Gnome to GNOME
 * Replaced icon with more proportional one
 * Update to GtkD 3.10.0
 * ci: Run Ubuntu builds in container as well
 * Change label of "view shortcuts" action
 * Clarify tooltip of "reset to default" button for keyboard shortcuts

Contributors:
 Aaron Honeycutt, Andrea Agosti, Arne Jørgensen, Eugene Ivanov,
 Felix Buehler, Jeremy Bicha, Jiehong Ma, Matthias Klumpp,
 Waldir Pimenta, Zsombor Welker, taoky

Version 1.9.5
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2022-02-22

Notes:
 * Tilix is still looking for a new maintainer!

Features:
 * Disable advanced paste when there is no linebreak like iTerm2
 * Add environment variable when in quake mode
 * Add possibility to configure always enabled regex

Bugfixes:
 * More appdata -> metainfo move
 * Add meson target for man page translations
 * Update flatpak manifest
 * meson: drop unused argument for i18n.merge_file()
 * Stop using deprecated Meson features
 * Keep quake window open if focus is restored before timeout has been reached
 * Don't check GtkDragResult (Wayland compatibility)
 * Don't add application/x-rootwindow-drop to dragSourceSet targets

Contributors:
 Alan Scherger, Antoine Belvire, David King, Jan Beich,
 kohnish, luk1337, matishadow, Winston Hoy, Matthias Klumpp

Version 1.9.4
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2021-02-10

Notes:
 * Tilix is looking for maintainers! At the moment, only very minimal maintenance is done,
   no new features will be implemented and pull-requests may be reviewed very slowly.

   If you are interested in helping Tilix, please chime in!

Features:
 * Actually install Yaru color scheme
 * Give every tab the ${title} (instead of "Default")
 * Add option to strip trailing whitespace on paste (#1904)

Bugfixes:
 * Fix saving of already saved session
 * Add shortcut to "Unselect all"
 * Many Meson buildsystem fixes
 * Avoid missing the previous command exit code when encoding URLs
 * Resolve some D deprecation messages
 * Mention powerline/fonts in README
 * Avoid calling `values()` on a shared object
 * Update metainfo data
 * Drop compat code for older D frontend versions
 * Bump minimum VTE version to 0.46
 * Remove deprecated Autotools support
 * Add release notes, NEWS file, automatic metainfo update
 * Update to GtkD 3.9.0

Translations:
 * This release contains many localization updates

